@startuml
title Grid Backtester - Core Detailed View with SaaS Black Box

' Compact visual architecture. Detailed file/interface inventory is in the side legend.
left to right direction

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam wrapWidth 95
skinparam maxMessageSize 90
skinparam nodesep 30
skinparam ranksep 22
skinparam defaultFontSize 10
scale max 2400 width

actor "User" as User

package "grid-backtest-saas\nblack box except important interfaces" as SaaS {
  component "REST/UI\n/api/v1/auth\n/api/v1/backtest\n/api/v1/research" as SaaSAPI
  component "Orchestration\nbacktest + research services" as SaaSOrch
  component "Async + Persistence\nDB session/models\nCelery worker" as SaaSInfra
}

folder "Market Data Files\nparquet/csv OHLCV" as MarketData
database "Metadata DB\nusers, runs, jobs" as DB
queue "Redis\nCelery broker/results" as Redis

artifact "Core Inputs\nconfigs + strategy + DataFrame" as Inputs

package "grid-backtest-core\nexpanded pure core" as Core {
  component "Public API + Contracts\nmodels, config, actions,\nDataSource protocol" as Contracts
  component "Simulation Engine\nBacktestEngine\nFast/Numba engine" as Engine
  component "Strategies + Policies\nIStrategy\nSimpleGrid\nDynamicGrid\nfilters/range/spacing/recenter/SLTP" as Strategies
  component "Execution + Indicators\nbootstrap\nconstraints\nreservations\nATR/EMA/RSI/ADX\nwarmup" as ExecInd
  component "Results + Research\nBacktestResult\ntrades/metrics/benchmark\nrepository utilities\ngrid search" as ResultsResearch
}

artifact "Core Outputs\nBacktestResult\nmetrics, trades,\nequity curve,\nresearch results" as Outputs

folder "SaaS Result File\nGRID_STORAGE_LOCAL_PATH/{run_id}.json" as SaaSResult
folder "Optional Core Exports\nsummary.json\ntrades.csv\nequity_curve.csv\nextra.json" as CoreExports

User --> SaaSAPI : REST/JSON
SaaSAPI --> SaaSOrch : validated requests
SaaSAPI --> SaaSInfra : auth/session/run metadata
SaaSInfra --> DB : ORM persistence
SaaSInfra --> Redis : async task state

SaaSOrch --> MarketData : read/filter/resample
MarketData --> Inputs : OHLCV DataFrame
SaaSOrch --> Inputs : build core configs\nand strategy

Inputs --> Contracts : public imports
Contracts --> Engine : domain/config/action types
Engine --> Strategies : IStrategy + EngineAction\nfill/cancel events
Engine --> ExecInd : bootstrap, constraints,\nreservations, indicators
Engine --> ResultsResearch : trades, metrics,\nbenchmark, research loop
ResultsResearch --> Outputs : result objects
Outputs --> SaaSOrch : return to app layer
SaaSOrch --> SaaSResult : write/read details
ResultsResearch --> CoreExports : optional export

' Layout nudges
SaaS -[hidden]right- MarketData
MarketData -[hidden]right- Inputs
Inputs -[hidden]right- Core
Core -[hidden]right- Outputs
Outputs -[hidden]right- SaaSResult

legend right
<b>SaaS visible files</b>
frontend/static/index.html, frontend/static/app.js
backend/app/main.py
backend/app/api/v1/auth.py, backtest.py, research.py, deps.py
backend/app/services/backtest_service.py, research_service.py
backend/app/db/models.py, session.py
backend/app/workers/celery_app.py, backtest_task.py
backend/app/core/config.py, security.py

<b>Exchanged inputs</b>
Market data: {SYMBOL}.parquet.gzip or {SYMBOL}_{timeframe}.csv
DataFrame: DatetimeIndex + Open, High, Low, Close, Volume
Core configs: BacktestConfig, IndicatorSpec, OrderExpiryConfig, WarmupConfig
Strategy configs: GridConfig, DynamicGridConfig

<b>Core files by component</b>
Contracts: __init__.py, models.py, config.py, engine_actions.py, data/protocols.py
Engine: engine.py, engine_fast.py, _numba_engine.py
Strategies: strategy/base.py, grid_simple.py, grid_dynamic.py, policies/*.py
Execution/indicators: execution/bootstrap.py, constraints.py, reservations.py, indicators.py
Results/research: results/models.py, trade_builder.py, metrics.py, benchmarks.py, repository.py, research/grid_search.py, grid_search_fast.py

<b>Core interfaces/events</b>
IStrategy.on_candle()
IStrategy.on_order_filled()
IStrategy.on_order_cancelled()
EngineAction: PLACE_ORDER, GRID_EXIT, CANCEL_OPEN_ORDERS
Events: OrderFilledEvent, OrderCancelledEvent
DataSource protocol: load(symbol,timeframe,start,end) -> DataFrame

<b>Generated outputs</b>
SaaS: GRID_STORAGE_LOCAL_PATH/{run_id}.json with metrics, benchmark_buy_hold, equity_curve[], trades[]
Core optional: summary.json, trades.csv, equity_curve.csv, extra.json

<b>Boundary rule</b>
Core has no FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, Redis/Celery, exchange SDK, or file data loader.
It receives in-memory configs/strategies/DataFrames and returns BacktestResult/research outputs.
endlegend

@enduml
